        <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">5. A Quick Checklist Before You Buy</h2>
        <p>
          Whichever use case matches your situation, run through this short
          checklist before finalizing a purchase. It catches the mistakes we
          hear about most often from readers after the fact.
        </p>
        <h3>Measure the Actual Storage Spot</h3>
        <p>
          Not the room in general, the exact corner, closet, or wall segment
          where the folded unit will live, including height clearance.
          "Folds up small" is relative, and the gap between a 27-inch and a
          36-inch folded width matters enormously in a tight space.
        </p>
        <h3>Confirm Your Weight Capacity Buffer</h3>
        <p>
          Never buy right at a machine's stated weight limit. Leave a
          comfortable buffer below the maximum, especially on the more
          compact machines in this guide, where lighter frame construction
          is part of how the smaller folded footprint gets achieved.
        </p>
        <h3>Match Deck Length to Your Height and Stride</h3>
        <p>
          If you're over roughly six feet tall or plan to run rather than
          walk, prioritize deck length over the smallest possible folded
          footprint. A compact machine that feels cramped mid-stride gets
          used less over time, no matter how easy it is to store.
        </p>
        <h3>Check What's Actually Included at the Price</h3>
        <p>
          Some folding treadmills require an ongoing app or coaching
          subscription to unlock their full advertised value. Factor that
          recurring cost into your real budget comparison before assuming
          the sticker price is the whole story.
        </p>

        <div class="not-prose bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-2xl p-6 my-8">
          <p class="font-black text-red-900 mb-3">Common Mistakes to Avoid</p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-red-800 text-sm">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-red-500 font-black">&bull;</span>
              Buying the smallest folded footprint available without
              checking whether the deck actually fits your height and
              stride.
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-red-500 font-black">&bull;</span>
